 {"id": "PEDS-U177", "ch": 22, "n": 1, "title": "Esophageal Atresia — Definition & Associated Anomalies", "sec": "Esophageal Atresia · p95", "qs": ["PEDS-C22-001", "PEDS-C22-002", "PEDS-C22-003", "PEDS-C22-004", "PEDS-C22-005", "PEDS-C22-006", "PEDS-C22-007", "PEDS-C22-008"], "guide": "Esophageal atresia = discontinuity in the esophagus. Associated anomalies: 1. Tracheo-esophageal fistula (TEF) — m/c defect in mesenchymal separation b/w trachea & esophagus; Gross classification A–F. 2. VACTERL association."},
